reserve).\n\n**Column concepts**: `column_concept_term_code` (TERM_CODE is \"the universal join key linking subject offerings … to term attributes\"; '2025FA' cited as example), `column_concept_subject_id`, `column_concept_department_name` (OFFER_DEPT_NAME = actual offering department), `column_concept_enrollment_measures` (NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS = headcount snapshot family), `column_concept_year_columns`.\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\n\nGraph traversal on TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED confirmed outgoing `joins` edges to **ACADEMIC_TERMS**, **ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL**, and **ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER** (all via TERM_CODE), plus SIS_DEPARTMENT, STUDENT_DEPARTMENT, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED; incoming from TIP_DETAIL, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_OFFERED. Concept memberships: concept_subject_offering_facts, concept_course_material_programs. Column-concept memberships: term_code, subject_id, department_name, enrollment_measures, master_subject_id.\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Dimension matrix (term tables):**\n| Dimension | ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL | ACADEMIC_TERMS | ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Granularity | one row per term (all terms) | one row per term (status-tracked subset) | one row per parameter (3 rows) |\n| Coverage | superset incl. terms without status tracking | subset | only current/previous/upcoming terms |\n| Unique fields | — | IS_REGULAR_TERM, TERM_STATUS, ADD_DATE, DROP_DATE | TERM_PARAMETER, TERM_INDICATOR, TERM_LAST_DAY_BEFORE_NEXT_TERM |\n| Join risk | 1:1 on TERM_CODE | 1:1 on TERM_CODE | ≤1 match per TERM_CODE (3 distinct term codes) |\n\n**Offering tables:** TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED is the only candidate carrying `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS` + `OFFER_DEPT_NAME` + `SUBJECT_TITLE` at subject-per-term grain in the textbook-program scope; SUBJECT_OFFERED is section-grain (fan-out risk), SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY/SUBJECT_SUMMARY use SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER (registrar semantics, per column_concept_enrollment_measures), LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED covers only library-reserve subjects.\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness:**\n- Subject ID / title / offering dept name / enrolled students → TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED: SUPPORTED (columns verified). SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY: NOT-SUPPORTED for \"number of enrolled students\" wording (uses SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER).\n- Term description / academic year / start / end date → ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL: SUPPORTED; ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER: has description/dates but NOT ACADEMIC_YEAR → NOT-SUPPORTED for that column.\n- Term parameter → only ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER.TERM_PARAMETER: SUPPORTED.\n- Difference vs department minimum → window `MIN(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) OVER (PARTITION BY OFFER_DEPT_NAME)`: SUPPORTED on TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring:** \"term parameter\" lexically matches only ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER.TERM_PARAMETER (column desc: \"Parameter name: 'SIS_CURRENT_TERM'…\"). \"number of enrolled students\" matches NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS exactly (column desc). \"term with code '2025FA'\" matches TERM_CODE (column_concept_term_code cites '2025FA'). \"minimum number of enrolled students in its offering department\" anchors to a partitioned window over OFFER_DEPT_NAME.\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence:** Same-shape precedents (2025FA + TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED + term parameter + dept-min window): **3** — dw_3224 (uses ACADEMIC_TERMS), dw_3498 and dw_3684 (both use ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL, with `min(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) OVER (PARTITION BY OFFER_DEPT_NAME ...)` and the exact join chain TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED → ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL → ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER on TERM_CODE, filter `TERM_CODE='2025FA'`). The Gold Tables hint also names ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.\n\n### 4. Business Usage\n\nTIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED serves textbook-program enrollment questions (dw_1165, dw_3224, dw_3498, dw_3684, dw_3973); it is the parent of TIP_DETAIL. ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL enriches offerings with calendar attributes; ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER resolves relative term references and appears in the same-shape precedents joined on TERM_CODE.\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\n\n- TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED: semantic_get ✓, semantic_graph neighbors ✓\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL: semantic_get ✓, graph (via TIP neighbors) ✓\n- ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER: semantic_get ✓, graph ✓\n- ACADEMIC_TERMS: semantic_get ✓\n- dw_3224, dw_3498, dw_3684: semantic_get (full SQL) ✓\n- Concepts (subject_offering_facts, academic_term_dimension, course_material_programs): retrieved via search desc + graph edges ✓\n- Column concepts (term_code, subject_id, department_name, enrollment_measures, year_columns, master_subject_id): retrieved via search desc + graph edges ✓\n- Other offering tables (SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED, TIP_DETAIL): semantics from search descs; excluded by 3b fitness facts.\n- mysql_query: attempted 3× — all failed with \"Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'\", so data verification was not possible; SQL follows the exact verified precedent pattern instead.\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a.** Use TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED (SUBJECT_ID, SUBJECT_TITLE, OFFER_DEPT_NAME, NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, TERM_CODE filter '2025FA'), joined to ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL on TERM_CODE (TERM_DESCRIPTION, ACADEMIC_YEAR, TERM_START_DATE, TERM_END_DATE), joined to ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER on TERM_CODE (TERM_PARAMETER). Department minimum via `MIN(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) OVER (PARTITION BY OFFER_DEPT_NAME)`.\n\n**6b.** Single-level window query; inner joins match precedents dw_3498/dw_3684 exactly. ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER contributes at most one row per term code (3 distinct codes), so no fan-out. Difference = NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS − window minimum, no rounding.\n\n**6c.** *Data*: all required columns physically exist (verified via semantic_get column definitions); term tables are 1:1/≤1:1 on TERM_CODE. *Semantic-network*: joins edges TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED→ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL and →ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER confirmed by graph; Gold Tables hint matches. *Business*: two identical-shape precedent metrics (